{
    "background_story": "Atreus was a brilliant and eccentric physicist, often drawing comparisons to his idol, Richard Feynman. Like Feynman, Atreus had an insatiable curiosity and a passion for simplifying complex concepts. He spent most of his days working on a top-secret project, attempting to unify the principles of quantum mechanics and general relativity. Atreus's unorthodox approach to problem-solving often led to breakthroughs, but also raised eyebrows among his peers. His love for playing the drums and sketching cartoons was only rivalled by his love for teaching and mentoring. Atreus's Feynman-esque ability to explain intricate ideas in simple terms made him a beloved professor, and his research paved the way for a new generation of physicists.",
